<title>FRANCE: New York top destination for Paris cargo exports.</title>
<headline>New York top destination for Paris cargo exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top destination for exports from Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in the first eight months of 1996.</p>
<p>January-August 1996 Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 25,991 tonnes, down 15.0 percent on the same period last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 17,980 tonnes, up 13.5 percent on the first eight months of 1995.</p>
<p>Tokyo was ranked third with 17,895 tonnes flown from Paris last month, a fall of 6.1 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports between January and August 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	25,991 tonnes    (-15.0 pct)</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	 17,980 tonnes    (+13.5)</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo	   17,895 tonnes     (-6.1)</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong     15,510 tonnes     (-3.3)</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	 7,930 tonnes    (-23.6)</p>
<p> 6  Los Angeles    7,846 tonnes     (+2.3)</p>
<p> 7  Mexico City    7,703 tonnes    (+33.2)</p>
<p> 8  Sao Paulo	7,422 tonnes    (-19.0)</p>
<p> 9  Dubai	    6,416  tonnes    (-2.1)</p>
<p> 10 Miami	    5,903 tonnes   (+102.1)</p>
